<section>
<title>LJ lj</title>
<p>This letter combination represents one sound, not a sequence of /l/+/j/. Do not pronounce it
as two consonants! It is a /j/-like /l/, as in <em>ball</em> (/ballj/, 'ball') in certain Norwegian
dialects. The sound can be long or short in Skolt Sámi; only the first letter is doubled. </p>

<table>
<tr>
<td><em class="lg_mat">viˊllj</em> 'brother'</td>
<td>PAS</td>
<td>PET</td>
<td>MUO</td>
<td>NOT</td>
<td>SUO</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><em class="lg_mat">šellj</em> 'yard'</td>
<td>PAS</td>
<td>PET</td>
<td>MUO</td>
<td>NOT</td>
<td>SUO</td>
</tr>
